{
  "note": "Fixture reference ranges for the lab trend (E09-01). Small on purpose: each band is one row of a published table, named by source id; the citations are under `sources`. Upper-only ranges read as 'under' (exclusive), lower-only as 'or more' (inclusive), two-sided ranges are inclusive at both ends. Ages are in years; `sex` null means either. A lab's own printed ranges, where a report names the lab, are under `labs` and win over the guideline for that analyte. These numbers stand in until a clinical reviewer signs off a licensed table, and the table needs a clinician's sign-off (LDL target, TSH age bands); nothing here is advice.",
  "sources": {
    "ncep-atp3-2001": "NCEP Expert Panel. Third Report of the National Cholesterol Education Program (Adult Treatment Panel III). JAMA 2001;285(19):2486-97, Table 2: total cholesterol <200 mg/dL desirable; LDL <100 optimal; HDL <40 low; triglycerides <150 normal.",
    "ada-soc-2024-s2": "American Diabetes Association. Standards of Care in Diabetes 2024, Section 2 (Diabetes Care 2024;47 Suppl 1:S20), Table 2.5: HbA1c below 5.7% is not in the prediabetes range.",
    "kdigo-2012-ckd": "KDIGO 2012 Clinical Practice Guideline for the Evaluation and Management of CKD. Kidney Int Suppl 2013;3(1), Figure 2: GFR categories G1-G2 are 60 or more mL/min/1.73m2.",
    "aacb-harmonised-2014": "Tate JR et al. Harmonised adult reference intervals for chemistry analytes (AACB/RCPA). Clin Biochem Rev 2014;35(4):213-35: potassium 3.5-5.2 mmol/L; creatinine male 60-110, female 45-90 umol/L.",
    "who-2011-haemoglobin": "WHO. Haemoglobin concentrations for the diagnosis of anaemia (WHO/NMH/NHD/MNM/11.1), 2011, Table 1: no anaemia at 13.0 g/dL or more in men, 12.0 g/dL or more in non-pregnant women.",
    "surks-hollowell-2007": "Surks MI, Hollowell JG. Age-specific distribution of serum thyrotropin in the US population (NHANES III). J Clin Endocrinol Metab 2007;92(12):4575-82: the upper TSH limit rises with age (about 4.0 under 70, 5.9 at 70-79, 7.5 at 80 and over, mIU/L); the lower limit stays about 0.4."
  },
